{
  // Editor + typecheck config. This is the config tsserver auto-discovers for every file
  // under `packages/nestjs` — both `src` and the relocated `test/` suite (INCLUDING
  // `*.integration.test.ts`); there is no nearer `tsconfig.json`, so this one owns them.
  // It must apply `experimentalDecorators` to those test files, otherwise the editor puts them in an
  // inferred project (no experimentalDecorators) and legacy 3-arg decorators like
  // `@Transactional` fail with TS1241 ("runtime will invoke the decorator with 2
  // arguments, but the decorator expects 3"). The root `tsconfig.test.json` fixes the CLI
  // typecheck but tsserver never reads it (it only discovers `tsconfig.json`).
  //
  // Why this shape (and not a composite test project + project references — the more
  // "canonical" TS pattern): `@drizzle-tx/core` is built by tsdown into a single bundled
  // `index.d.ts`, NOT by tsc into per-file composite declarations. Project references
  // require tsc-emitted per-file output to redirect into, so a composite test project that
  // references the packages fails with TS6305/TS6310 under the repo's load-bearing
  // `tsc -b --noEmit` typecheck. So test ownership is handled per-package here instead.
  //
  // `noEmit` + non-composite (no `rootDir`) on purpose: the tests live under `test/` (outside
  // `src`) and import the shared harness (`../../../../test/**`, `../../../../vitest.*`), so a
  // `rootDir: "src"` emit config would reject both with TS6059. Emit is handled by
  // the sibling `tsconfig.build.json` (node16, `rootDir: src`, excludes tests), which is
  // what the `build` script and the root `tsc -b` solution reference.
  //
  // `moduleResolution: bundler` (not node16): the integration tests statically import the
  // ESM harness, but this package is `"type": "commonjs"`, so node16 would flag them TS1479
  // ("cannot require an ES module"). Those tests never run under Node's CJS resolver —
  // vitest (SWC) bundles them — so bundler mode models their real runtime. Strict node16
  // CJS semantics for the shipped `src` are enforced by `tsconfig.build.json`.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2023",
    "lib": ["ES2023"],
    "module": "preserve",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "experimentalDecorators": true,
    "emitDecoratorMetadata": true,
    "useDefineForClassFields": false,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "composite": false,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src", "test"],
  "exclude": ["**/*.test-d.ts", "dist"]
}
